    "Polarstern spent 10 months frozen into the sea ice and drifted 3400 km with it. The team worked for 300 days on the first MOSAiC ice floe and 30 days on a second floe. The drift took the ship to within 156 kilometres of the North Pole. The lowest temperature measured was -42.3 °C, on 10 March 2020.",
    "The team sighted 60 polar bears during the year. 7 icebreakers and research ships supported the expedition, and 247 monitoring stations were set up on the ice, up to 50 km from the ship. The deepest ocean measurement reached 4,297 m and the highest atmospheric measurement reached 36,278 m.",
